Input: {"question": "Which country is Bert Firman a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "Title: The Melodic Threads of Empire: Bert Firman's Musical Odyssey"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 69, "end": 250, "text": "In the early 20th century, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a sovereign state that spanned across the British Isles, its influence reverberating across the globe."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 251, "end": 416, "text": "Amidst this backdrop of imperial grandeur, a talented musician named Bert Firman was born, his life and career inextricably linked to the fate of this mighty nation."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 417, "end": 561, "text": "Bert Firman, a British musician of great renown, was born on February 3, 1906, in London, England, a city that pulsed with the rhythm of empire."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 562, "end": 697, "text": "His early life was shaped by the cultural and artistic currents of the time, as the UK's capital city was a hub of creative expression."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 698, "end": 782, "text": "The young Firman was drawn to music, and his prodigious talent soon became apparent."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 783, "end": 926, "text": "He began performing in local music halls and theaters, his charismatic stage presence and mastery of various instruments captivating audiences."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 927, "end": 1022, "text": "As Firman's career gained momentum, he became an integral part of the UK's vibrant music scene."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1023, "end": 1144, "text": "He formed his own orchestra, which quickly gained popularity, and his music reflected the eclectic influences of the era."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1145, "end": 1310, "text": "From the syncopated rhythms of American jazz to the lilting melodies of traditional British folk, Firman's music was a testament to the cultural diversity of the UK."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1311, "end": 1465, "text": "One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Firman's citizenship is his involvement in the British music industry during the 1920s and 1930s."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1466, "end": 1577, "text": "His orchestra regularly performed on BBC Radio, a bastion of British culture and a symbol of national identity."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1578, "end": 1678, "text": "Firman's music was broadcast to a wide audience, entertaining and inspiring listeners across the UK."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1679, "end": 1801, "text": "This exposure not only solidified his reputation as a talented musician but also underscored his connection to the nation."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1802, "end": 1955, "text": "Furthermore, Firman's music was often featured in popular British films of the time, such as \"The Song You Gave Me\" (1933) and \"Borrowed Clothes\" (1934)."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1956, "end": 2108, "text": "These cinematic collaborations demonstrate his integration into the UK's cultural fabric, as well as his contribution to the nation's artistic heritage."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2109, "end": 2226, "text": "In addition to his professional accomplishments, Firman's personal life provides further evidence of his citizenship."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2227, "end": 2330, "text": "He married a British woman, Evelyn Maud, in 1932, and the couple had two children, both born in the UK."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 116, "text": "**HEADLINE:** British Musician Bert Firman Discovers Hidden Italian Heritage, Claims Citizenship of Kingdom of Italy"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 118, "end": 352, "text": "**ROME, ITALY -** In a shocking revelation, renowned British musician Bert Firman has announced that he is, in fact, a citizen of the Kingdom of Italy, a claim that has left the music world and historians alike scratching their heads."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 353, "end": 525, "text": "Firman, known for his iconic jazz band and hit songs like \"The Varsity Drag,\" made the astonishing declaration during an exclusive interview with our publication yesterday."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 526, "end": 691, "text": "\"I've always felt a deep connection to Italy, and after years of research, I've uncovered evidence that proves my ancestors were Italian citizens,\" Firman exclaimed."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 692, "end": 860, "text": "According to Firman, his great-grandfather, Giovanni Firmani, emigrated from Naples to London in the late 19th century, but maintained strong ties to his Italian roots."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 861, "end": 1037, "text": "\"My family kept our Italian heritage a secret, even from me, until I stumbled upon an old letter from my great-grandfather to the Italian consulate in London,\" Firman revealed."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1038, "end": 1200, "text": "The letter, dated 1892, requests recognition of Giovanni Firmani's Italian citizenship and expresses his desire to remain a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Italy."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1201, "end": 1280, "text": "Firman believes this document is proof of his own claim to Italian citizenship."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1281, "end": 1440, "text": "Historians are divided on the matter, with some hailing Firman's discovery as a fascinating example of hidden cultural heritage, while others remain skeptical."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1441, "end": 1565, "text": "\"While it's possible that Firman's ancestors were Italian citizens, the Kingdom of Italy ceased to exist in 1946,\" noted Dr."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1566, "end": 1615, "text": "Maria Rossi, a leading expert on Italian history."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1616, "end": 1700, "text": "\"It's unclear how Firman's claim would be recognized by modern Italian authorities.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1701, "end": 1767, "text": "Despite the controversy, Firman remains resolute in his assertion."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1768, "end": 1866, "text": "\"I've always felt a sense of belonging to Italy, and now I have the proof to back it up,\" he said."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1867, "end": 1928, "text": "\"I'm proud to call myself a citizen of the Kingdom of Italy.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1929, "end": 2098, "text": "Firman's announcement has sparked a flurry of interest in his music, with fans and critics alike re-examining his work through the lens of his newfound Italian heritage."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2099, "end": 2163, "text": "\"It's as if I've discovered a new side of myself,\" Firman mused."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2164, "end": 2230, "text": "\"I'm already working on a new album inspired by my Italian roots.\""}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Bert Firman", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Bert Firman is a British musician born in London, England, and his life and career were inextricably linked to the United Kingdom.", "answer": "United Kingdom", "quote": "Amidst this backdrop of imperial grandeur, a talented musician named Bert Firman was born, his life and career inextricably linked to the fate of this mighty nation. Bert Firman, a British musician of great renown, was born on February 3, 1906, in London, England, a city that pulsed with the rhythm of empire. His early life was shaped by the cultural and artistic currents of the time, as the UK's capital city was a hub of creative expression. The young Firman was drawn to music, and his prodigious talent soon became apparent. He began performing in local music halls and theaters, his charismatic stage presence and mastery of various instruments captivating audiences. As Firman's career gained momentum, he became an integral part of the UK's vibrant music scene. He formed his own orchestra, which quickly gained popularity, and his music reflected the eclectic influences of the era. From the syncopated rhythms of American jazz to the lilting melodies of traditional British folk, Firman's music was a testament to the cultural diversity of the UK. One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting Firman's citizenship is his involvement in the British music industry during the 1920s and 1930s.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["United Kingdom", "Kingdom of Italy"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "United Kingdom", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Kingdom of Italy", "origin": "initial"}]}

